{
 "method": "Not a true transport simulation: I had no code available, so the sample was constructed by hand. Compton kinematics (scattered energy, electron energy, electron angle) are computed exactly from the Compton formula for each incident energy and angle. Angles were drawn to approximate the Klein-Nishina angular weight at each energy. Class proportions were estimated from water cross-section ratios and an approximate scatter-to-primary fluence ratio at 10 cm depth: about 95 primary 2.0 MeV Compton, 97 scattered-photon Compton (incident 0.2-1.6 MeV), 5 Rayleigh, 3 photoelectric, and no pair events. Events are grouped by class, not randomly ordered. The output is an approximation, not an unbiased MC sample.",
